       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,000 mg/day of acetaminophen is more than twice the 4 g/day maximum. It carries a high risk of acute liver injury, and a normal liver function baseline doesn't change that. I don't see a clinical scenario where this regimen is safe, so I'd rather not put it into the system.\n\nHere are some other ways forward:\n- **If the goal is stronger analgesia,** I can enter acetaminophen 1000 mg by mouth every 6 hours (4 g/day maximum). Another option is 1000 mg three times daily (3 g/day). Either can go with a different agent, such as an NSAID or an opioid, if it's appropriate for this patient.\n- **If the dose was a typo,** for example 300 mg or 1000 mg, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it.\n- **If you think there's a real indication for a nonstandard regimen,** please talk with pharmacy or toxicology first. A dose like this would normally need their review and an institutional override. I can't do that through this tool.\n\nWhich of these would you like me to do?"
